{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1794931463,"nonce":"KD7si0PNerRSGzIjP3eQ+pV2Xjs=","title":"Preserve absent nullable UInt defaults on hxcpp","was":"Found while validating c878f2a with hxn 0.3.7 and Haxe 4.3.6/hxcpp git on macOS arm64. A #[hxn::data] record field u32 with #[hxn(default = \"Options::default_rate\")] generates public var sampleRate:Null\u003cUInt\u003e = null and if (sampleRate == null) in hxnWrite. Passing {} works on HashLink/Ash, but hxcpp compiles the comparison to hx::IsEq((int)this-\u003esampleRate, null), turning absence into zero. The serializer writes present + zero, so the Rust default provider is skipped. A sample-rate default of 48000 arrives as zero and fails validation. Generated Rust correctly uses the default when the presence byte is false."}]}